{
  "title": "Names That Mean Strength",
  "seoTitle": "Names That Mean Strength: Girl, Boy and Unisex Names",
  "description": "Over 70 real names that mean strength, strong or mighty, from Matilda, Audrey and Valerie to Ethan, Gabriel and Fergus, each meaning sourced.",
  "section": "meanings",
  "published": "2026-11-13",
  "motif": "hammer",
  "intro": "<p>Strength is one of the commonest ideas in old names, because names were often made to wish a child courage or power. Old English and Old German built many from a few words for strength: <em>þryþ</em> in Audrey and Mildred, <em>drud</em> in Gertrude, <em>hart</em> ('hardy, brave') in Richard, Leonard and Bernard. Hebrew has Ethan ('firm, enduring') and Gabriel ('God is my strong man'), and Latin has Valerie and Valentina. Every meaning here is checked against a cited source, mostly Behind the Name, with England and Wales ranks from the ONS.</p><p>A few names are usually listed as 'strength' on thin evidence. Brian and Bridget may or may not have a 'power' root, and Boaz and Amos don't mean strength at all. Those are marked uncertain.</p>",
