  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "The Old English and German strength words",
      "content": "<p>A small set of words turns up again and again. Old English <em>þryþ</em> ('strength') ends Audrey (Æthelthryth), Mildred and Elfreda. Its German cousin <em>drud</em> ends Gertrude, Hiltrud and Ortrud. Old German <em>hart</em>, 'hard, brave, hardy', ends Richard, Leonard, Bernard and Gerard. If you spot one of these at the end of an old name, you can be fairly sure strength is part of the meaning.</p>"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Choosing a nickname",
      "content": "<p>Many strength names are long and old-fashioned, and come with friendly short forms. Matilda gives Tilly or Tilda, Gertrude gives Gertie or Trudy, Millicent gives Millie, and Valentina gives Val or Tina. Ezekiel shortens to Zeke and Hezekiah to Hez. It's worth trying the short form with your surname too.</p>"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Strength names in the Bible",
      "content": "<p>Several Hebrew names carry the idea of God giving strength: Ezekiel ('God will strengthen'), Hezekiah ('Yahweh strengthens'), Uzziah ('my power is Yahweh') and Gabriel ('God is my strong man'). Ethan, 'firm, enduring', is the simplest, and it has been one of the most used boys' names in England and Wales for years.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "faqs": [
    {
      "question": "What girl name means strength?",
      "answer": "Matilda and Maud ('strength in battle'), Audrey ('noble strength'), Mildred ('gentle strength'), Gertrude ('spear of strength'), Valerie and Valentina ('strong'), and Thrud (Old Norse, 'strength')."
    },
    {
      "question": "What name means strength of God?",
      "answer": "Gabriel means 'God is my strong man', Ezekiel 'God will strengthen' and Hezekiah 'Yahweh strengthens' in Hebrew. Uzziah means 'my power is Yahweh', and Chike, from Igbo, 'God of strength'."
    },
    {
      "question": "What name means strength in Hebrew?",
      "answer": "Oz means strength, Eyal 'might, strength' and Adir 'strong, mighty'. Ethan and its modern form Eitan mean 'solid, enduring, firm'."
    }
  ],
